|~ `::excerpt`, the kind of the facts a host tells of a failure past its
   rooms, and what is declared under it: its laws.
   The rules it holds: [QSPRN#excerpt], [QSERR#alert]. ~|

:excerpt
  |~~ An excerpt tells the facts of a failure a host prints past the room
      of a fact, under the tag of its refusal, `::X::excerpt{…}`: each fact
      whole within three hundred characters, and past them the cell the
      host keeps it in, `:actualValue ::cell"…"`, beside the views the kind
      of the fact reveals that fit the room, each under the name of the fact
      and its own, `:actualValue/count 3410`; a host that keeps no cell
      shows the views alone. Nothing is cut: a fact stands whole, as a cell
      that gives it back whole, or as the facts its kind reveals of it.

      An excerpt is a map under its tag, read by its keys, and the kind of
      the refusal over it reads its facts by their names, a cell standing
      for any fact; `raise` refuses it, a failure told and not held. The
      whole is read live, a fact of a failure by `!|` and a cell by
      `answer`.
      ::link~(::kind/reveals | doc) ::link~(::cell | doc)
      ::link~(::qlang/hosts | doc)
  ~~|
  ::kind
    | accepts |~~ The facts told, whole, as cells or as views. ~~| ::map
    | throws :PayloadKindNotTakenError
        |~~ An excerpt is the map of the facts a host tells of a failure,
            `::X::excerpt{:actualValue ::cell"…" :actualValue/count 3410}`.
        ~~|
    | proves :readsBackAsItself
        |~~ An excerpt prints and reads back as itself. ~~|
        ~(::excerpt{:actualValue ::cell"f410f1df625c" :actualValue/count 3410} | :e it | print | parse | open | eq e)
    | proves :readsAViewByItsKey
        |~~ A view stands under the name of its fact and its own. ~~|
        ~(::excerpt{:actualValue/count 3410} | get /:actualValue/count | eq 3410)
